#descr "Shalarin settlements were located within the Lower Depths of Serôs, between 600 and 1200 feet below the surface and could dive twice as deep. Only tritons, krakens and a few others were able to survive at such depths. Shalarin developed specialized means of growing kelp beyond the normal reach of the sun, and were exceptionally gifted cultivators of pearls, which drove their economy and which they crafted into extraordinary works of art as well as weapons of war. Like most aquatic races, shalarin rarely wore clothes because of the drag it created while swimming. Most wore nothing more than a belt or harness made of woven kelp, sea snake skin, or eelskin.

The shalarin were originally found in the Sea of Corynactis, far from Faerûn's shores. The Demon Lord, Dagon, was responsible for their arrival in Serôs, using potent magic to transport a vast number of shalarin to the Inner Sea via a one-way portal known as the Wildtide Gate. Once they arrived, merfolk and aquatic elven servants of the demon lord were instructed to slaughter them. The plot was almost a total success as 8 in 10 shalarin were massacred. The Dukar Orders intervened in the final days of the conflict, saving the race from extinction and eventually driving the demon-worshippers to the Serôsian fringe. However, the shalarin of Serôs were completely cut off from their gods and the handful of their kin who remained in hiding in Corynactis. Dagon has continued his plotting ever since and eventually succeeded in subsuming the shalarin gods. 

3 millennia later, the shalarin have managed to carve an empire out of the Lower Depths of Serôs. Known as As'arem and comprised of four kingdoms - Es'rath, Es'purr, Es'roch, and Es'daan - the shalarin have become a key power center within the Inner Sea. Generally well liked by others, they always display impeccable manners and respect. They are seen as an indispensable ally in the war to come with Iakhovas the Ravager and his sahuagin armies." 
