#nametype 275
#descr "The Seekers Caste - also called the Currents of shalarin culture, simultaneously existed both within and outside of shalarin society. Upon the completion of their training they were expelled from settlements and were required to explore the world beyond to gather knowledge of people and places the shalarin did not know. The caste was made up of both the Wanderers and the Faiths sub-castes.  

Shalarin were generally very private about their religious beliefs and practices. They were teleported to Serôs from their native lands far across the Trackless Sea by Dagon, who hoped to silence their gods. Four times, he sent the Shalarin to the inner sea. Those who came in the First and Second Passings quickly discovered that their gods no longer answered their prayers, for though unknown to them, Dagon had succeeded in killing and taking over the portfolios of the shalarin pantheon. None of the original shalarin knew the cause of the Passings, and some priests continued to worship their old gods, believing the silence to be a test of faith. 

Those who came in the Third and Fourth Passings knew no native gods, and joined the shalarin born in Serôs in who were beginning to explore the more responsive Faerûnian deities. Eldath, Persana, Istishia, and Mystra were the most commonly revered, while Deep Sashelas, Eadro, Milil, Oghma, and even Umberlee also enjoyed a notable number of worshippers." 
