#name "Nantari Cavalier Captain"
#descr "The Nantari Cavaliers were the elite mounted forces of Myth Nantar. Blessed by the priests and bolstered by the high mages of the City of Destinies, the Nantari Cavaliers upheld The Laws of Battle across Serôs. These captains are also adept at communicating with and training Sacred Dolphins to accompany their forces.

Wars in Serôs were rare – only 11 true wars had occurred since -10,000 DR. Conflict was typically a contained, calculated affair and rarely went beyond border skirmishes and hunting raids. This wasn’t because the region was peaceful, but rather because their wars were so disastrous.  Major conflicts among two initial parties easily drew in all allies, not to mention the frenzy they caused among the sea life. The hunters and scavengers that the battle-dead attracted, and the difficulties of restoring these wild creatures to their natural habitats, were one of many reasons that the races of Serôs agreed to limit their wars. The conventions they adopted were known as the Laws of Battle. They prohibited spilling blood on sacred ground, for example, and prohibited battles taking place more than once in a tenday so that the dead could be collected. There were many others. 

Myth Nantar upheld these laws, and patrolled the entire sea with the help of the Nantari Cavaliers. When Myth Nantar’s mounted forces were strong, the realms beneath the sea flourished – a fact not forgotten by the city’s leadership when wisdom prevailed."
